    "bodyText": "Explore Log In Data Science Machine Learning Build AI Apps with ChatGPT, Dall-E, and GPT-4 Instructor: Tom Chant Enroll Starts Jul 28 Access provided by Digital Education Development Centre 442,661 already enrolled 6 modules Gain insight into a topic and learn the fundamentals. 4.7 1,736 reviews Intermediate level Recommended experience Flexible schedule 4 hours to complete Learn at your own pace 96% Most learners liked this course About Modules Testimonials Reviews What you'll learn The basic concept of AI Engineering How to build apps with the OpenAI API How to deploy your AI apps on the web Skills you'll gain Real Time Data AI Security AI Integrations Cloud Deployment Responsible AI Application Deployment Serverless Computing LLM Application Artificial Intelligence Multimodal Prompts Tools you'll learn Generative AI Web Development Tools Web Applications Prompt Engineering Model Deployment Frontend Integration ChatGPT Application Programming Interface (API) OpenAI OpenAI API Details to know Shareable certificate Add to your LinkedIn profile Assessments 6 assignments Taught in English 22 languages available See how employees at top companies are mastering in-demand skills Learn more about Coursera for Business There are 6 modules in this course This course teaches web developers to build apps using OpenAI's API, helping them take their first steps as an AI Engineers. Learners will get hands-on practice with both the GPT-4 and Dall-E APIs, using OpenAI's JavaScript SDK. In the first project, MoviePitch, you will get a primer on the OpenAI API and harness the power of artificial intelligence to generate ideas and images. In our second project, KnowItAll, we’ll move to the ChatGPT-4 model and get to grips with building chatbots - one of the most common uses of AI for web devs. Finally, we will fine-tune our chatbot in the third project. Fine-tuning is where you upload a dataset to OpenAI and use it to train a model. Doing this allows the chatbot to answer questions specific to your data - a critical skill when working with AI. Read more 🟨 Intro to AI Engineering 01 - Foundations and API Basics Module 1 • 1 hour to complete Module details 🟨 Intro to AI Engineering 02 - Advanced Topics and Applications Module 2 • 1 hour to complete Module details 🟨 Test your AI Engineering Knowledge – Graded Assignment Module 3 • 1 hour to complete Module details 🟦 Deploying your AI App 01 - Security and API integration Module 4 • 1 hour to complete Module details 🟦 Deploying your AI App 02 - Advanced Features and Deployment Module 5 • 29 minutes to complete Module details 🟦 Test your AI Deployment Knowledge Module 6 • 1 hour to complete Module details Instructor Instructor ratings 4.3 ( 336 ratings ) Tom Chant Scrimba 11 Courses • 469,205 learners Offered by Scrimba Learn more Why people choose Coursera for their career Felipe M. Learner since 2018 \"To be able to take courses at my own pace and rhythm has been an amazing experience. I can learn whenever it fits my schedule and mood.\" Jennifer J. Learner since 2020 \"I directly applied the concepts and skills I learned from my courses to an exciting new project at work.\" Larry W. Learner since 2021 \"When I need courses on topics that my university doesn't offer, Coursera is one of the best places to go.\" Chaitanya A. \"Learning isn't just about being better at your job: it's so much more than that. Coursera allows me to learn without limits.\" Learner reviews 4.7 1,736 reviews 5 stars 85% 4 stars 7.94% 3 stars 2.98% 2 stars 1.12% 1 star 2.93% Showing 3 of 1736 S SR 4 · Reviewed on Jul 18, 2025 not very practical at the end using Cloudflare and Polygon; rest were very good A AB 4 · Reviewed on Jul 30, 2025 A great course to start building AI Apps but I found one thing that lacked, and it's nothing is provided that's downloadable, like transcript etc. S SO 5 · Reviewed on Oct 24, 2023 excellent course within, plus great tutor overall. View more reviews Coursera Footer Skills Professional Certificates Courses & Specializations Career Resources Coursera Community More © 2026 Coursera Inc. All rights reserved.",
